      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): move settings navigation into sidebar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nSettings pages mix route-level horizontal settings navigation with page-local width and overflow behavior. This makes General, Channels, Debug, Logs, Appearance, and related Settings pages feel inconsistent, and some pages can keep wider or nested-scroll layouts than the rest of Settings.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nIn this PR, Settings route navigation moves into a Settings-only sidebar with grouped existing Settings routes, sidebar search, and a Back to OpenClaw exit. Settings pages also share a 980px content workspace, while only the outer clipped config wrapper that created nested scrolling is removed.\n\nLanguage/control reorganization is intentionally deferred, and internal card styling is preserved.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers get a consistent Settings workspace across existing Settings routes, can search and jump between Settings pages from the sidebar, and can leave Settings with an explicit Back to OpenClaw action. This is a layout/navigation change only.\n\n## Evidence\n- `git diff --check`\n- `corepack pnpm ui:i18n:check`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/app-navigation-groups.test.ts ui/src/app-navigation.test.ts ui/src/pages/config/view.browser.test.ts`\n- `corepack pnpm ui:build`\n- Browser smoke on mock Control UI: `/config`, `/channels`, `/debug`, `/logs`, and `/appearance` used the Settings-only sidebar, hid normal sessions/footer chrome, removed the old horizontal Settings route nav, and inherited the 980px workspace.\n- Search smoke: typing `logs` in the Settings sidebar returned the Logs entry and did not open the global command palette.\n- Mobile smoke at 390x844 on `/logs`: Settings sidebar and Back to OpenClaw were visible.",
        "branch": "brzezowski/settings-layout-sidebar",
        "head_sha": "1f438373e2f25db28309d1b8723bf889cf8adc8d",
